<h1>ARMS — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Effective date: 1 November 2026</p>
<p>ARMS is a local-first, open-source AI agent gateway. It runs on your
machine and connects your agents to the services you choose — mail, code
hosting, chat, databases, and file stores — under a policy you control.
Each connector accesses only the service it names, and only to perform
the actions you ask your agents to perform.</p>
<h2>Data we access</h2>
<p><strong>Connectors in general:</strong> a connector reads and writes
through the account credentials you place in ARMS's encrypted vault. ARMS
routes agent tool calls to that service; it does not copy your service
data to any operator.</p>
<p><strong>Gmail connector:</strong> with your consent via Google OAuth,
the Gmail connector requests Gmail read, modify, compose, and send
scopes. It accesses message content, labels, threads, and drafts only to
perform the actions you ask your agents to perform.</p>
<h2>Where your data lives</h2>
<p><strong>Self-hosted / open-source use:</strong> your service data and
OAuth tokens stay on machines you control — an encrypted local vault,
plus a database you choose (your own MongoDB Atlas or Aiven PostgreSQL).
There is no ARMS-operated server in this mode; we cannot see, access, or
share your data because it never reaches us.</p>
<p><strong>Cloud tier (if offered):</strong> your data is stored per-tenant in
isolated databases with per-tenant encryption keys, used only to operate the
service.</p>
<h2>What we never do</h2>
<p>We never sell your data, never share it with advertisers, never use it
to train models, and never access more of a service than the task you
requested requires. Deleted mail is moved to Trash (recoverable for 30
days); ARMS never permanently deletes mail or service data on its own.</p>
<h2>Your controls</h2>
<p>Revoke a connector's access at the service — for Gmail,
<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>&nbsp;(this
immediately stops the Gmail connector). Delete local data by removing the ARMS
state directory; request cloud-tier deletion by
<a href="https://github.com/jayptl-me/arms-site/issues">opening an issue</a> and we confirm within
30 days.</p>
